     MocaccinoOS v26.11 release
---

Hello everybody!

We’re excited to announce the release of MocaccinoOS v26.11.

We hope you enjoy this release and the improvements it brings.

With kind regards,

Ettore Di Giacinto  
Joost Ruis  
Mihai Dobrescu  
Jerrod Frost

### Changes since 26.10

- Kernel upgraded to 6.18.60 (LTS)
- Mesa version 26.2.6

### Issues and improvements

- Installer: you can now choose how swap is handled during installation
- Layers, apps and ISO images now ship a package list
- Improved config file handling: updates are now merged automatically in most cases. This was prompted by the eMudhra CA compromise, where an updated ca-certificates had to reach users reliably
- linux-firmware and its split packages updated
- Kernel groundwork for sched_ext (scx) schedulers, so alternative CPU schedulers can be offered in a future release
- Still testing optional [x86-64-v3 optimized](https://www.mocaccino.org/blog/2026/08/05/new-optional-x86-64-v3-builds-zero-risk-for-everyone-else/) builds for improved performance on supported modern CPUs

### Help Us Improve MocaccinoOS

You can extend your system with additional software using Flatpak, Docker, or the community repository.
We welcome your feedback — whether it's bug reports or ideas for improvement.

Explore our [documentation](https://www.mocaccino.org/docs/) to learn more.

### Project sustainability note

MocaccinoOS is currently supported by community donations totaling **approximately $1 per month**.
While development continues, this level of funding is not sufficient to sustainably support long-term work.

If you find MocaccinoOS useful and would like to help keep the project healthy, consider supporting us via donations.

https://www.mocaccino.org/docs/donate/

### Acknowledgement
MocaccinoOS builds on the incredible work of the Gentoo Linux community. We are grateful for their efforts, and all packages are compiled on our own infrastructure powered by Kairos

### Available editions

MocaccinoOS v26.11 is available in five desktop editions: KDE Plasma, XFCE, GNOME, MATE, and COSMIC.

Whether you prefer a modern, feature-rich desktop, a lightweight environment, a traditional layout, or a fresh and innovative desktop experience, there’s an edition to suit your workflow.

All editions share the same MocaccinoOS foundation, giving you a consistent approach to software management and system updates, with the freedom to choose the desktop experience that works best for you.

### Download

Check out our [download page](https://sourceforge.net/projects/mocaccino/files/) for all recent releases.